menu "zlib Configurations"
    config ZLIB_PREFER_PSRAM
        bool "Prefer PSRAM for zlib's own allocations"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            Route the memory zlib allocates for a deflate/inflate stream
            through heap_caps, so its large working buffers can live in PSRAM.
            Internal 8-bit RAM is used as a fallback when PSRAM is not
            initialized or cannot satisfy an allocation. Requests below 16 KiB
            keep preferring internal RAM.

            The gzip file APIs (gzopen, gzread, gzwrite) still use malloc()
            for their own state and I/O buffers.

            Only the allocator a z_stream uses for its own state and buffers
            is affected. The compression and decompression buffers an
            application passes in are its own, and are allocated by the
            application.

            A custom allocator installed in z_stream.zalloc/zfree always wins
            over this option, as zlib documents.
endmenu
